Made every string the add-on renders translatable. The login page, the callback, the first-login wait, the identities list, the user-menu entry, the OAuth client panel and the secret reveal all formatted their text as literal English; only the two control-panel containers went through `react-intl`. All of them now define their messages and format them, so a site can translate this add-on like any other, and the extracted catalogues carry the full set.

Nothing a reader sees changed in English: each message keeps as its `defaultMessage` the exact text the component used to hard-code. Tests render through a new `testing` helper that supplies the `IntlProvider` the components now require. @ericof
